<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE policymap [
  <!ELEMENT policymap (policy)*>
  <!ATTLIST policymap xmlns CDATA #FIXED ''>
  <!ELEMENT policy EMPTY>
  <!ATTLIST policy xmlns CDATA #FIXED '' domain NMTOKEN #REQUIRED
    name NMTOKEN #IMPLIED pattern CDATA #IMPLIED rights NMTOKEN #IMPLIED
    stealth NMTOKEN #IMPLIED value CDATA #IMPLIED>
]>
<!--
  Hardened ImageMagick policy for the Dédalo TS media engine (foundation audit
  MEDIA-02). Loaded via MAGICK_CONFIGURE_PATH (set by engine/imagemagick.ts).

  Dédalo converts raster images here and NOTHING ELSE that needs a second program.
  This policy removes the classic ImageMagick/Ghostscript RCE / SSRF /
  file-disclosure vectors that Dédalo never needs: the PostScript/EPS/XPS coders,
  the scripting coders (MSL/MVG), remote-fetch delegates (URL/HTTP/HTTPS/FTP), and
  @-indirection.

  THE GHOSTSCRIPT DELEGATE IS DENIED (2026-09-05, audit MEDIA-01). It used to be
  the one delegate left enabled, because ImageMagick cannot read a PDF without it
  and Dédalo needs the PDF cover. A delegate, though, is a process the ENGINE never
  spawns: it inherits neither the resource block below nor the `-limit` argv, and
  it is not the process our request cap kills. Measured on a 441-byte PDF declaring
  a 200000x200000-point page: with both MEDIA-01 halves armed, `magick` sat
  bounded while its `gs` child grew an intermediate towards 120 TB, and after
  `kill -9` of the magick we spawned, gs REPARENTED TO PID 1 and kept running
  (+8.8 MB/min, one core) with nothing in the engine able to reap it. So Dédalo
  now spawns Ghostscript ITSELF (src/core/media/engine/ghostscript.ts): the page
  box is read with poppler first, a page above the configured pixel ceiling is
  refused before anything renders, the render runs under the spawn discipline's
  cap, and the process the cap kills IS the one doing the work. The engine hands
  ImageMagick the resulting PNG. Denying `gs` here is what makes that the ONLY
  route — including for the ImageMagick runs this engine did not build.

  Every ImageMagick process in the engine loads this file — conversions through
  runMagickTo AND reads through runIdentify (engine/binaries.ts), because
  ImageMagick selects its coder from the file CONTENT: measured 2026-08-04,
  `identify -ping` on a `.png` holding PostScript reports `PS` and exits 0
  unpoliced, and is refused here.

  RESOLVED 2026-08-08 — the SVG note below stands as the REASON, not as a gap.
  ImageMagick is no longer asked to rasterize SVG at all: `engine/svg.ts` renders
  the vector with librsvg (`rsvg-convert`) and hands the PNG to the thumb recipe,
  so the MVG coder stays disabled and component_svg still gets its thumbnail. Do
  not "fix" the thumb by relaxing the rule below.

  WHY THAT DECISION HAD TO BE MADE (measured 2026-08-04): on a build with no
  librsvg delegate, ImageMagick RASTERIZES
  an SVG through its own MSVG renderer, which emits MVG — so `coder MVG rights
  none` also blocks every SVG→raster conversion:
    magick 'x.svg[0]' -background '#ffffff' -flatten -thumbnail 222x148 out.jpg
    → "not allowed by the security policy `MVG'", exit 1, no file
  PROBING an SVG is unaffected (identify -ping reads the header only). The choice
  was between requiring a librsvg delegate and narrowing the policy; requiring
  librsvg won, as a DEDICATED renderer rather than an ImageMagick delegate — a
  program that parses SVG and nothing else has no coder dispatch to reach.

  RESOURCE CEILINGS (2026-09-05, audit MEDIA-01). The coder/delegate denials above
  bound WHAT ImageMagick may parse; they bound nothing about HOW MUCH it may
  allocate. A 40000x30000 solid-colour TIFF is a few MB on the wire, passes the
  magic-byte sniff, and decodes to 14.4 GB RSS (measured, engine/probe.ts) on the
  AUTHENTICATED UPLOAD REQUEST PATH — a denial of service by a legitimate-looking
  heritage file. The `domain="resource"` block below is the HARD CEILING: an
  ImageMagick process cannot raise a resource above a policy value, only below it
  (measured — `-limit width 300000` under `width 200000` here fails with "cache
  resources exhausted"). It is deliberately GENEROUS, because a large-format map
  scan is a real heritage artefact and the ceiling must not refuse one.

  THE OPERATING LIMITS ARE ARGV, NOT THIS FILE: `magickResourceLimitArgs()`
  (engine/binaries.ts) splices `-limit` into every ImageMagick argv from the
  DEDALO_MAGICK_LIMIT_* catalog keys, so an install tunes its own bound without
  editing a shipped file, and this ceiling is what an install cannot exceed. Both
  halves are required: the policy also binds the ImageMagick invocations this
  engine does not build (a delegate child, an operator's shell), which no argv can
  reach. Gate: test/unit/magick_policy_tripwire.test.ts.

  A SEQUENCE IS NOT A PIXEL CACHE, which is why `list-length` is in the block too
  (2026-09-05): `-ping` reads headers and allocates no pixels, but it still
  enumerates every SCENE of a multi-image source, so a 4.6 MB GIF declaring 200000
  one-pixel frames cost a HEADER READ 26.3 s and 8.73 GB RSS with every limit above
  armed — on the upload preview path. It is the one row here that bounds a probe.

  MEMORY/MAP/AREA/DISK DEGRADE; WIDTH/HEIGHT/TIME/LIST-LENGTH REFUSE. Exceeding the pixel-cache
  budgets moves the cache to disk (slower, still correct); exceeding width, height
  or time kills the run, which is why those three are the ones an install may
  legitimately need to raise for an outsized master.

  NO DELEGATE RESIDUE: the one process this block could not reach was the
  Ghostscript delegate, and it is denied above — the engine spawns gs itself,
  refusing an oversized page before the render and killing the render it started.
  What remains outside every bound here is the HOST's own share of a legitimate
  large conversion (cgroup/systemd), which is an ops decision, not a converter one.
-->
<policymap>
  <!-- Ghostscript: DENIED, the engine spawns gs itself (see the header). -->
  <policy domain="delegate" rights="none" pattern="gs" />
  <policy domain="delegate" rights="none" pattern="ps:alpha" />
  <policy domain="delegate" rights="none" pattern="ps:cmyk" />
  <policy domain="delegate" rights="none" pattern="ps:color" />
  <!-- Remote fetch / SSRF via delegates -->
  <policy domain="delegate" rights="none" pattern="URL" />
  <policy domain="delegate" rights="none" pattern="HTTP" />
  <policy domain="delegate" rights="none" pattern="HTTPS" />
  <policy domain="delegate" rights="none" pattern="FTP" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="URL" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="HTTPS" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="HTTP" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="FTP" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="MSL" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="MVG" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="TEXT" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="SHOW" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="WIN" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="PLT" />
  <!-- PostScript family: the CVE-2018-16509 class. Dédalo never processes PS/EPS/XPS. -->
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="PS" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="PS2" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="PS3" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="EPS" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="EPT" />
  <policy domain="coder" rights="none" pattern="XPS" />
  <!-- Indirect reads via @filename in arguments -->
  <policy domain="path" rights="none" pattern="@*" />
  <!-- Resource ceilings (MEDIA-01) — the HARD ceiling an install cannot exceed. -->
  <!-- The OPERATING limit is DEDALO_MAGICK_LIMIT_*, spliced as -limit argv. -->
  <!-- Keep every comment in this element on ONE LINE: measured 2026-09-05, a -->
  <!-- MULTI-LINE comment inside policymap makes ImageMagick's parser drop -->
  <!-- every policy after it (magick -list policy showed zero resource rows). -->
  <policy domain="resource" name="memory" value="8GiB" />
  <policy domain="resource" name="map" value="16GiB" />
  <policy domain="resource" name="area" value="8GiB" />
  <policy domain="resource" name="disk" value="64GiB" />
  <policy domain="resource" name="width" value="200000" />
  <policy domain="resource" name="height" value="200000" />
  <policy domain="resource" name="time" value="1800" />
  <!-- list-length: how many IMAGES one source may hold. The ONLY row here that -->
  <!-- bounds a header-only read: -ping skips pixels but still enumerates every -->
  <!-- scene, and a scene struct is not the pixel cache, so memory/map/area/disk -->
  <!-- never see it. Measured 2026-09-05: a 4.6 MB GIF of 200000 1x1 frames cost -->
  <!-- identify -ping 26.3 s / 8.73 GB RSS with every limit above armed; under a -->
  <!-- list-length of 4096 the same file is refused at 180 MB. -->
  <!-- NO BACKTICK MAY APPEAR IN A COMMENT IN THIS ELEMENT: measured 2026-09-05, -->
  <!-- a backtick makes ImageMagick drop every policy that FOLLOWS the comment -->
  <!-- (this very row read back as unlimited), exactly like a multi-line one. -->
  <policy domain="resource" name="list-length" value="65536" />
</policymap>
